\paragraph{Complex-domain effective coverage (B1 audit).}
A domain-coverage audit (10 seeds $\times$ 10 scenarios $\times$ 4 configurations, $n=400$) measured the effective domain coverage $C_{\mathrm{eff}} = |\text{domain}| \times \text{SR}$ on the complex tier. Results: Rule $1.933$ [1.800, 2.000]; LLM+heuristic $1.987$ [1.960, 2.000]; LLM+MAPPO $1.668$ [1.474, 1.873]; Pure MAPPO $0$ (SR floor). The complex tier's effective coverage is roughly half that of the medium tier, consistent with the cross-tier SR gap. The high-fidelity 14-scenario B1 coverage audit was not completed before the submission deadline; the 14-scenario effective coverage is therefore not claimed as a finished deliverable.
\paragraph{Baseline-strength diagnostic (E14).}
Because the complex tier's pure-MAPPO success rate is 0\%, we ran a frozen-scenario diagnostic re-training audit (12 configurations $\times$ 3 training seeds, continuous mode, 8 envs, 4096 steps/rollout, goal-injection probability 0.5; inference by the deterministic actor without goals; seed-bootstrap 95\% CIs, 3 independent training seeds, 20k resamples): doubled training length (10M steps), medium-weight curriculum (weight init only, optimizer/reset-normalizer reinitialized), and two hyperparameter sweeps (halved LR; doubled LR with doubled entropy). All best and final confirmation success rates remain 0\% across all 12 configurations. Critically, a frozen \emph{medium}-tier checkpoint transfers directly to complex at 50\% pre-check success (5/10) yet collapses to 0\% after on-complex fine-tuning. Together this is evidence of training dynamics---policy forgetting under on-complex goal injection and distribution shift---not task unsolvability; the boundary claim of Section~6.2 rests on the deployment outcome (layering shows no net advantage), not on this causal attribution. A structural intervention (simplified complex re-training) was not executed, as it requires changing frozen scenario parameters and separate authorization.

\paragraph{Headroom-manipulation feasibility probe (Experiment 2).}
Section~6.7 notes that the negative side of P3 cannot be tested as a within-family information gradient; this paragraph records the probe behind that claim. All runs use the scripted rule planner only (no LLM calls), on the IE-05 multi-axis family, with the same execution tier and metric field, so the probe isolates the planning layer.
Two studies were run; they manipulate different variables and are never merged. \emph{Study 1} (existing frozen gate data, seeds 4151--4160, 4 quantity tiers $\times$ 10) contrasts allocation-decision rules at a fixed strong dose: $greedy{=}\mathrm{true}$ vs.\ $greedy{=}\mathrm{false}$. The difference is positive in 4/4 tiers (range $+0.012$ to $+0.106$; 2/4 exclude zero), i.e., allocation-rule quality contributes on the order of $+0.1$. \emph{Study 2} (new runs, seeds 64101--64105) contrasts planning-information availability: full plans vs.\ degraded (hold) plans, after a 32-tier baseline scan located near-saturated tiers (scan range $0.17$--$1.00$). The full-vs-degraded effect is significant in 5/5 tiers, magnitude $+0.62$ to $+0.73$---an order of magnitude larger than allocation-rule quality, and a successful positive control for the information manipulation. A granularity probe (N013, seed 64101) confirms the manipulation is effectively binary: removing only \texttt{target\_id} from the goal collapses the tier to $\approx 0.18$, while removing position/speed/pattern/constraints changes nothing ($0.9692$ in both cases), because the executor consumes only \texttt{target\_id}.
The 2$\times$2 interaction is \emph{not} attributable to headroom, for three reasons that must accompany any citation: (i) the degraded arm is a structural floor---$V \approx 0.18$ across all tiers, insensitive to tier and seed, so it carries no difficulty fingerprint; (ii) the tiers split by scan $V$ do not differ by pre-registered difficulty; (iii) all seed-level variance comes from the full-information arm, making the interaction descriptive only. Combined with Study 1, the family separates the contributions cleanly---plan availability ($\approx 0.7$) vs.\ allocation-rule quality ($\approx 0.1$)---yet its headroom dimension is not resolvable by information-level manipulation, which is why condition (iii)'s causal evidence is carried by the cross-family contrast of Section~6.7 rather than a within-family information gradient. Data: \texttt{e1\_2x2\_option1.json}, \texttt{e1\_2x2\_option2.json}; Study 2 batch SHA-256-manifested (594 files).

